ds":["*"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Saʿy is brisk walking, used for eagerness to meet; it contrasts with the self-sufficient person’s aversion to receiving the Prophet’s attention.","anchor":"والسعي : شدة المشي ، كني به عن الحرص على اللقاء فهو مقابل لحال من استغنى","mentions":["80:5"]},{"verses":["80:9"],"words":["*"],"type":"grammar","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The clause is circumstantial; the object of ‘fears’ is omitted because it is understood as fear of God in scriptural usage.","anchor":"وجملة { وهو يخشى } في موضع الحال ، وحذف مفعول { يخشى } لظهوره لأن الخشية في لسان الشرع تنصرف إلى خشية الله تعالى","mentions":[]}]}
